   <refbody>    <section>
      <p>This API request includes the following query and header parameters.</p>
      <ul id="ul_10492777">
         <li>Query Parameters:</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The query parameters are added to the end of the request URL to provide additional information to the server.</p>
    </section>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
         <tgroup cols="4">
            <colspec colname="c1"/>
            <colspec colname="c2"/>
            <colspec colname="c3"/>
            <colspec colname="c4"/>
            <tbody>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Parameter</b>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Type</b>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Description</b>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Required</b>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>continuationToken</entry>
                  <entry>string</entry>
                  <entry>Requests the next set of results. If more records are available, then a continuation token will be returned. For example, eyJwayI6ImFkaybSIsInNrIjoxNTkyMIyNDUyLCJ0ZW5hbnRJZCI6ImFkaSJ9</entry>
                  <entry>No</entry>
               </row>
            </tbody>
         </tgroup>
      </table>
    <section>
      <ul id="ul_10492778">
         <li>Header Parameters:</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The header parameters instruct the API on handling requests, such as authentication and compressing responses over 1KB.</p>
    </section>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
         <tgroup cols="5">
            <colspec colname="c1"/>
            <colspec colname="c2"/>
            <colspec colname="c3"/>
            <colspec colname="c4"/>
            <colspec colname="c5"/>
            <tbody>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Parameter</b>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Type</b>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Description</b>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Input Value</b>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Required</b>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>Authorization</entry>
                  <entry>string</entry>
                  <entry>Authenticates API requests. Provide a valid bearer token in the HTTP header. This bearer token can be obtained from the <xref href="../access_the_api/oauth.dita" format="dita">OAuth bearer token request</xref>.</entry>
                  <entry>N/A</entry>
                  <entry>Yes</entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>Accept-Encoding</entry>
                  <entry>string</entry>
                  <entry>Compresses responses. Responses over 1KB in size will automatically be compressed. The client must be capable of receiving and decompressing the response. Warning: The header is not set; responses greater than 1 KB will fail.</entry>
                  <entry>gzip: Compression format using the Lempel-Ziv coding (LZ77), with a 32-bit CRC. deflate: Compression format using the zlib structure and deflate compression algorithm. br: Compression format using the Brotli algorithm.</entry>
                  <entry>Yes</entry>
               </row>
            </tbody>
         </tgroup>
      </table></refbody>
</reference>
